# onnxruntime-node's postinstall downloads the CUDA 12 execution-provider
# binaries (libonnxruntime_providers_{cuda,tensorrt,shared}.so) from
# api.nuget.org on every linux/x64 install. Nothing here can use them: the
# encoder creates its InferenceSession with no `executionProviders`, so ORT runs
# on the CPU provider, which ships bundled inside the npm package. The download
# was several hundred megabytes of dead weight on every `npm ci` in every
# workflow.
#
# It was also a single point of failure outside our control. Run 31914828013
# (nightly refresh, 2026-08-15) died in `npm ci` with ETIMEDOUT connecting to
# api.nuget.org — no feeds polled, no ingest, no publish. A retry loop would
# only have made the pointless download more patient.
#
# npm exposes this to lifecycle scripts as npm_config_onnxruntime_node_install,
# which onnxruntime-node's parseInstallFlag() reads before doing any network
# work. Applies to every workspace and every workflow, so there is nothing to
# keep in sync per job.
onnxruntime-node-install=skip
